{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Stand now.</b> [The form is] second person [feminine singular]." "<b>With your spell-casters.</b> A noun in plural form, derived from 'and a charmer of charms' [in] וחובר חבר (Deuteronomy 18:11)." "<b>To profit.</b> A verb [rather than a noun]." "<b>Perhaps you will terrify.</b> Derived from עריץ (Isaiah 29:20)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:27.087205880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}